    "answer_type": "decomposition",
    "summary": "The energy bill increased by \u20ac166,526.43 (71.0%) this quarter, rising from \u20ac234,538.17 to \u20ac401,064.60.\n\nThe increase is primarily driven by external factors:\n- Tariff changes: \u20ac91,740.36 (39.12%)\n- Weather effects: \u20ac27,407.84 (11.69%)\n- Product mix: \u20ac22,546.75 (9.61%)\n- Volume: \u20ac20,667.05 (8.81%)\n\nControllable waste accounted for \u20ac4,164.42 (1.78%) of the increase. A specific finding identifies a persistent off-production load on \"compressors_2\" (excess of 9.02 kW), consistent with a compressed-air leak. Physical inspection is recommended.\n\nAssumptions and limitations: The baseline model has a 6.0% holdout MAPE. The waste component is an unexplained residual; asset-level claims are based on corroborating meter evidence. Attribution uses Shapley values, and tariff impacts are calculated per 15-minute interval.",
